{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Attaching your own data","anchor":"Attaching-your-own-data","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)","doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/removeAttachmentProvider(_:)","doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachmentProvider","doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment","doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipReportContext"],"generated":true}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenClipKit"}],"role":"article","title":"Attaching your own files"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Add your app’s own state to every report, so the agent sees what the screenshot can’t show.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/AttachingYourOwnFiles"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/attachingyourownfiles"]}],"kind":"article","sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Your app knows things ScreenClip can’t see: the signed-in account, what’s in the cart, which feature flags are on, the last request the backend answered. Register an attachment provider and its files travel with every report, next to the built-in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/Diagnostics","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["#if DEBUG","ScreenClipKit.setAttachmentProvider(\"cart\") { context in","  let cart = await MainActor.run { CartStore.shared.snapshot }  \/\/ any Encodable","  return [try .json(cart, name: \"cart\", summary: \"the cart's \\(cart.items.count) items and promo codes\")]","}","#endif"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The agent reads each file’s name and summary in its prompt. It opens a file only when the screenshot and note aren’t enough, so write the summary for it: say what is inside.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"When the provider runs","type":"heading","anchor":"When-the-provider-runs","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The provider starts when the report sheet opens, not when the tester taps ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Send"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Its data matches the screen the tester captured, not whatever the app shows a minute later.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Slow work, such as a network call, a database read, or a file on disk, overlaps the time the tester spends marking up."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Send"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", ScreenClip waits up to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timeout"},{"type":"text","text":" more (5 seconds by default, at most 30) with "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Saving report…"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" on screen. It then sends the report without whatever hasn’t arrived."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The provider runs off the main actor. Read main-actor state with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await MainActor.run { … }"},{"text":", and keep heavy work out of that closure.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Several files, async work, and context","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Several-files-async-work-and-context"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A provider returns any number of attachments. Return an empty array to add nothing this time.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["ScreenClipKit.setAttachmentProvider(\"account\", timeout: .seconds(10)) { context in","  let session = await MainActor.run { Session.current }","  guard let session else { return [] }","  let flags = try await FeatureFlags.shared.current()","  APILog.shared.mark(\"ScreenClip report \\(context.reportID)\")","  return [","    try .json(session.debugSummary, name: \"account\", summary: \"signed-in account, plan, and region\"),","    .text(flags.description, name: \"feature-flags\", summary: \"remote feature flags in effect\"),","    .text(await APILog.shared.recent(20), name: \"api-requests\", summary: \"last 20 backend requests and status codes\"),","  ]","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipReportContext"},{"type":"text","text":" carries the report’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reportID"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"capturedAt","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screenTitle"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screenPath"},{"text":". Log the report id next to your own records, such as a backend request id or an analytics session, to tie them to the report.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Cancellation and failure","level":3,"anchor":"Cancellation-and-failure"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The provider is cancelled when the tester cancels the report, or turns off "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Attach logs and diagnostics","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":". Use cancellable APIs or check "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task.isCancelled"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the provider throws or misses its timeout, only its own files are left out. The report is still sent, and a line is logged under the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenClipKit"},{"type":"text","text":" subsystem."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Registering and removing","level":3,"anchor":"Registering-and-removing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each id holds one provider. Registering the same id again replaces it, so calling "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" from an initializer or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onAppear"},{"type":"text","text":" is safe. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/removeAttachmentProvider(_:)"},{"text":" removes it. Providers run concurrently, and their files are listed in registration order.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Names and limits","level":3,"anchor":"Names-and-limits"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"name","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" becomes a file name the Mac accepts. It is lowercased, anything other than letters, digits, and "},{"code":"-","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" becomes "},{"code":"-","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and it is cut to 32 characters, plus "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".txt"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".json"},{"type":"text","text":". A name already in use, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"logs.txt"},{"type":"text","text":" or another provider’s, gets "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-2"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-3"},{"type":"text","text":", and so on."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each attachment can be up to 1 MB (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment\/maximumBytes","isActive":true},{"text":"). Larger ones are left out.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All files in a report share a 4 MB limit. When a report is over it, the largest files are dropped first."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","text":"What not to attach","level":3,"anchor":"What-not-to-attach"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Don’t attach secrets. On the Mac, token-like strings are hidden in text files, but JSON files are stored as sent. Any attached file can be read by an agent working on the report.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In Release builds "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" does nothing, and the closure is never called. Keep the call inside "},{"code":"#if DEBUG","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" anyway, so the code that gathers the data stays out of Release too."}]}]}],"references":{"screenclip-icon.svg":{"variants":[{"traits":["1x","light"],"url":"\/images\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/screenclip-icon.svg"}],"alt":"The ScreenClip icon","identifier":"screenclip-icon.svg","type":"image"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipReportContext":{"url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipreportcontext","title":"ScreenClipReportContext","abstract":[{"text":"What a provider knows about the report it is attaching to.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipReportContext","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenClipReportContext"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenClipReportContext"}]},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/Diagnostics":{"role":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The optional files ScreenClipKit attaches, and how the tester controls them."}],"title":"Diagnostics","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/Diagnostics","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/diagnostics"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipAttachment/maximumBytes":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximumBytes","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The largest attachment ScreenClip sends. Larger ones are left out of the report."}],"title":"maximumBytes","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment\/maximumBytes","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipattachment\/maximumbytes"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit":{"role":"collection","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Report what you see in your own iOS app, straight into ScreenClip on your Mac, where a coding agent fixes it."}],"title":"ScreenClipKit","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit","images":[{"identifier":"screenclip-icon.svg","type":"icon"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipAttachmentProvider":{"url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipattachmentprovider","title":"ScreenClipAttachmentProvider","abstract":[{"text":"Collects your app’s own attachments for a report. It runs off the main actor; read main-actor","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state with ","type":"text"},{"code":"await MainActor.run { … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Throwing leaves this provider’s files out of the report.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachmentProvider","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenClipAttachmentProvider"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenClipAttachmentProvider"}]},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipAttachment":{"url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipattachment","title":"ScreenClipAttachment","abstract":[{"text":"A file your app adds to a report, next to ScreenClip’s own logs and diagnostics.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenClipAttachment"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenClipAttachment"}]},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipKit/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipkit\/setattachmentprovider(_:timeout:_:)","title":"setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Adds your app’s own files to every report: state, records, anything an agent would want"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to see next to the screenshot."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"setAttachmentProvider"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"timeout"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","text":"Duration"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13ScreenClipKit0aB18AttachmentProvidera","text":"ScreenClipAttachmentProvider"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipKit/removeAttachmentProvider(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipkit\/removeattachmentprovider(_:)","title":"removeAttachmentProvider(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Stops adding the files from the provider registered with ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/removeAttachmentProvider(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"removeAttachmentProvider"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic"}}}